---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Digitali privacy policy: what this website collects, what the offline planner does with your data, and your rights."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="section-tight legal">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width: 780px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

      <div class="draft-banner" role="note">
        <strong>DRAFT — owner must review before launch.</strong> This is a
        plain-language draft, not legal advice. Company details marked
        [MERCHANT CONFIG] must be filled in, and a qualified professional should
        review this document for your jurisdiction. Last updated: October 2026.
      </div>

      <p>
        This policy covers two different things: <strong>(1)</strong> this
        website ({site.canonicalUrl}), and <strong>(2)</strong> the downloadable
        planner software. They handle data very differently, so we describe them
        separately.
      </p>

      <h2>1. This website</h2>
      <h3>What we collect</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact messages:</strong> if you email us, we receive your name,
          email address and message content so we can reply. We use it only for
          that purpose.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Payments:</strong> when checkout is activated, payment processing
          is provided by Lemon Squeezy as Merchant of Record. They collect and
          process payment information under their own privacy policy. We do not
          receive or store your card details.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h3>What we do not collect on this site</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          There is currently <strong>no analytics, no advertising tracking and no
          cookies</strong> set by this website. If that changes, this policy will
          be updated before any tracking begins.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. The downloadable planner</h2>
      <p>
        The planner is an offline HTML file that runs entirely in your browser. It:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>stores your planning data <strong>locally on your device</strong> (IndexedDB with a localStorage fallback);</li>
        <li>makes <strong>no network requests</strong> — no analytics, no tracking, no cloud sync, no external fonts or scripts;</li>
        <li>
          never transmits your data to us or to anyone else. There is no technical
          mechanism by which we could see it.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Because your data lives in your browser, clearing browser/site data will
        remove it. The planner includes a manual JSON export so you can keep your
        own backups — we recommend using it regularly.
      </p>

      <h2>Data retention and your rights</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Contact emails are kept only as long as needed to handle your request.</li>
        <li>
          Depending on your jurisdiction [MERCHANT CONFIG: jurisdiction], you may
          have rights to access, correct or delete personal data we hold about
          you. Contact us to exercise them.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Controller</h2>
      <p>
        [MERCHANT CONFIG: legal company name], [MERCHANT CONFIG: registered
        address]. Contact: [MERCHANT CONFIG: contact email].
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we change this policy, we will update the "last updated" date above.
        Material changes will be announced on this site before they take effect.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
